MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_001: This statue used to be surrounded by joy and smiling\nfaces. I'm glad Lord Solel can't see it now...
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_002: Oh, Promsy! I didn't expect to see you here.
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_003: <NCA>"Why are you cleaning?"
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_004: I guess I feel like I owe it to Lord Solel. It's really\nthe least I can do.
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_005: <NCA>"You owe it to Solel? Why is that?"
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_006: <NCB>"The least you can do?"
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_007: <ACA>I just do. Though...I doubt he knew much about\nme at all.
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_008: <ACB>Honestly, I wasn't ever able to do much more than\nthis, and I'm not sure it mattered all that much.
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_009: Believe it or not, the work here at the temple didn't\nalways come naturally to me. I messed up. A lot.
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_010: The older priests made me feel bad about having\npoor etiquette or not cleaning things correctly.
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_011: Looking back, I probably shouldn't have taken their\nadvice so hard and just kept at it.
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_012: But no, I'd get riled up and chew myself out even\nmore. And then mess up all over again!
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_013: One day I was hiding in a corner, crying about my\ncountless mistakes, when Lord Solel spotted me.
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_014: He must've felt sorry for me, because he tried to\ncheer me up. He even bought me something to eat!
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_015: I was so touched by his kindness that I burst into\ntears. I got my food all soggy and salty...
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_016: Don't get me wrong, it was still delicious! I just wish\nI'd had one more chance to eat with him again...
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_017: <NCA>"Is it really such a precious memory?"
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_018: It is. But whenever I think about it I get a little sad\nbecause that was it. I'll never see him again.
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_019: Poor Lord Solel... I wish you were still alive.
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_020: People say he's to blame for what's going on right\nnow. They say he had it coming and deserved to die.
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_021: He was treated like a traitor—buried who knows\nwhere—but I refuse to think anything bad about him.
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_022: He was kind to a no-name like me in his temple,\nnever mind that she was a constant screwup.
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_023: I just don't believe someone like that would allow the\nworld to fall to ruin.
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_024: Oh! Who am I to say that? I'm still a nobody.\nI know, I know...
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_025: <NCA>"I'm sure Solel would appreciate your words."
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_026: Thank you. I'd like to believe that. And when you\nsay it, I almost do.
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_027: You must be a big fan of Lord Solel too, huh?
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_028: Ngh...
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_029: Oh! You aren't?
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_030: Then you never knew Solel at all, Promsy! Don't\nworry. I know all sorts of good stories about him.
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_A_031: I spoke with him only once, but I've read every\nbook I could find about him. I'm a reeeal expert!
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_S: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_S_001: Huh? Mm...
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_S_002: P-Promsy? Is that you? I never thought I'd get a\nchance to thank you!
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_S_003: So...thanks! For saving the world, I mean. I'm sure\nLord Solel would be grateful too.
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_S_004: <NCA>"I didn't do it alone."
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_S_005: <NCB>"We all worked together!"
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_S_006: Aw, Promsy...
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_S_007: Ehehe. That's nice of you to say. You're going to\nmake me cry again.
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_S_008: I wonder, would you be interested in helping me\nbuild Lord Solel's shrine? If you have time...
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_S_009: I'm probably doing it more for me than him. I have\nno idea if this is what he'd want.
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_S_010: I just think he deserves a grand and beautiful tomb\nfit for a Divine Sovereign.
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_S_011: Once this shrine is built, everyone will finally know\nhow great he truly was.
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_S_012: <NCA>"I can't remain here very long..."
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_S_013: <NCB>"There's somewhere I must go."
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_S_014: <ACA>I figured. And this will take quite some time.
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_S_015: <ACB>I know... There are people all over the world that\nneed your help.
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_S_016: Sorry to put you on the spot like that, Promsy. \nI knew it'd be a lot to ask...
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_S_017: Hey, quit with the sad puppy face. I'm sure Lord\nSolel would've said the same thing.
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_S_018: You love Dagda, and you need to do everything you\ncan to keep it safe.
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_S_019: I get that. But it doesn't make saying goodbye\nany easier.
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_S_020: But, every hello leads to goodbye, doesn't it?\nThat's just life, I suppose!
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_S_021: I won't let myself be sad too long.
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_S_022: I've got too much to do, getting this shrine built. It's\ngoing to outshine all the temples!
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_S_023: Everyone will know how good—and great—Lord\nSolel was. Remember? I'm a reeeal expert!
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_S_024: Hehe. I guess we both have a lot to do,\ndon't we?
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_S_025: <RSDS>Come back here someday and see the shrine,\nwon't you, Promsy? I hope you'll like it!
MID_SE_Ism_Sop_S_026: Then I'll treat you to a nice banquet too! Oh, I can't\nwait to hear all about your adventures!